      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.93,
      "end_seconds": 10.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.94,
      "end_seconds": 28.7,
      "duration_seconds": 16.76,
      "text": "um, uh, so... cramping pain in the lower tummy that's why I came i did try to ignore it for a while i just want to get back to normal, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.56,
      "end_seconds": 33.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.49,
      "end_seconds": 40.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "About... well, nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.36,
      "end_seconds": 46.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "I follow. Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.78,
      "end_seconds": 57.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "I'd say severe. I notice it more with stress. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.2,
      "end_seconds": 76.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.89,
      "end_seconds": 80.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, uh, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.24,
      "end_seconds": 100.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.56,
      "end_seconds": 105.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I take Colospa, when it cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.68,
      "end_seconds": 111.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.58,
      "end_seconds": 116.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "not really, you know, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.16,
      "end_seconds": 125.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.06,
      "end_seconds": 131.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.65,
      "end_seconds": 134.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.16,
      "end_seconds": 140.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.94,
      "end_seconds": 146.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.78,
      "end_seconds": 150.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.43,
      "end_seconds": 155.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fever or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.63,
      "end_seconds": 161.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "no fever or night-time diarrhoea, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.53,
      "end_seconds": 169.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Have you had any family history of bowel cancer or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.44,
      "end_seconds": 173.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.52,
      "end_seconds": 181.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.68,
      "end_seconds": 183.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.52,
      "end_seconds": 188.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.85,
      "end_seconds": 193.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.18,
      "end_seconds": 207.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.8,
      "end_seconds": 223.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.45,
      "end_seconds": 261.29,
      "duration_seconds": 22.84,
      "text": "okay: BP is 109 over 78, saturation 97 percent, temperature is 36.7 degrees and pulse is 83 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18. Right, here's what I'm thinking my working impression is irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis that's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.42,
      "end_seconds": 265.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Right, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.77,
      "end_seconds": 276.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.49,
      "end_seconds": 302.91,
      "duration_seconds": 15.42,
      "text": "I'll request a coeliac test, it'll help with bloating. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.5,
      "end_seconds": 313.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "Mm, okay. See me again after the results are back. Right, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.62,
      "end_seconds": 322.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.58,
      "end_seconds": 328.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.38,
      "end_seconds": 332.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "So, alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
